                      (a) Definitions.

                      "Control" means the power, direct or indirect, to cause
                      the direction and management of an entity, whether by
                      contract, ownership of fifty percent (50%) or more of
                      its outstanding shares or voting rights, or otherwise.
                      An entity is "Controlled" when subject to Control, and
                      entities are "Under Common Control" when subject to the
                      same Control.

                      "Revenue Threshold Entity" means any entity, together
                      with all entities it Controls or is Under Common Control
                      with, whose annual revenue was at least one billion
                      United States dollars (US$1,000,000,000) in any of
                      calendar years 2026, 2027, or 2028.

                      "Production Environment" means any deployment or use of
                      the Licensed Work in a live environment serving real
                      business workloads, whether internal or on behalf of
                      third parties, and excludes development, testing,
                      quality-assurance, staging, and evaluation use.

                      (b) Any entity that is not a Revenue Threshold Entity
                      may make any use of the Licensed Work, including
                      production use.

                      (c) A Revenue Threshold Entity may make internal
                      non-production use of the Licensed Work. Without a
                      separate license from the Licensor, a Revenue Threshold
                      Entity may NOT: (i) use the Licensed Work in a
                      Production Environment; or (ii) use or distribute the
                      Licensed Work, alone or incorporated into another
                      product or service, in connection with offering that
                      product or service to third parties.

                      (d) Where a product or service incorporating the
                      Licensed Work is supplied to a third party, the
                      restrictions in clause (c) apply to the supplier that
                      incorporates or distributes the Licensed Work; the
                      recipient of that product or service is not subject to
                      clause (c) solely by reason of receiving or using that
                      product or service as supplied.

